  "fields": {
    "title": "Command-Line Interface",
    "textContent": {
      "data": {},
      "content": [
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Description",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "The term command-line interface (CLI) refers to the use of command lines for the interaction of a human with a computer, which is one way of human-computer interaction (HCI). In this process, lines of text are passed to the computer either directly via the keyboard or in the form of a script, which the computer then executes.\nCLI is the historical ancestor of the ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "1DDBuJHPyDiiT0BOAEo8V6",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "graphical user interface (GUI)",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": ", although command lines also exist among graphical user interfaces.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Background",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Command lines were historically the first and only methods of interaction with the operating system. The terminal originates from around the 1950s-60s and its original form really does not resemble what we use today. In many operating systems, the command line is nowadays evaluated by a shell or a command line interpreter. Command lines only require text mode, but are also available in graphics mode with modern operating systems, for example as terminal emulation.",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Usage",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "heading-3"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "The command-line interface is still often used to start or install programs. You don't need to use it,  you can also use a mass of extensions that can be used as a proxy to use terminal commands. But for more complex tasks it is quite useful to use the terminal. On the Mac it’s intuitively called ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "value": "Terminal",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": ", while on Windows it is called ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "value": "cmd.exe",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": ". Some ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "target": {
                  "sys": {
                    "id": "5iDbuNsGpFL1VgEDoXhyHo",
                    "type": "Link",
                    "linkType": "Entry"
                  }
                }
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "code editors",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "entry-hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " like ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [
                {
                  "type": "italic"
                }
              ],
              "value": "visual studio code",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": " let you also access the terminal inside their editor. To launch the terminal on a Mac:",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "Open Finder -> Applications -> Utilities -> Terminal",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "data": {},
          "content": [
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "The terminal makes it possible to easily install dependencies needed to develop with modern frontend frameworks like react, vue, svelte, etc. The most common tasks for frontend development involve the node package manager (",
              "nodeType": "text"
            },
            {
              "data": {
                "uri": "https://www.npmjs.com/"
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "data": {},
                  "marks": [],
                  "value": "npm",
                  "nodeType": "text"
                }
              ],
              "nodeType": "hyperlink"
            },
            {
              "data": {},
              "marks": [],
              "value": "). ",
              "nodeType": "text"
            }
          ],
          "nodeType": "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "nodeType": "document"
    },
